            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "John Kelley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great and simple. A word of warning: Do NOT use a smokey BBQ sauce with lil smokeys. Use a sweet bbq sauce."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "catlover1952"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been making these for years. The only thing I do differently is mix equal parts grape jelly, BBQ sauce and ketchup. This also works just as well with cut up beef hot dogs. Adults and kids alike love these. I love them especially because they're fast, easy and can be prepared in advance.",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-15T01:53:17.397Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Greg Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made these many times. I use only Hillshire Farms Beef Lil Smokes. I use 6 packages in a 6 quart crockpot and cook on low for about 4 hrs, then switch to warm if needed. I use the 8 oz. jar of grape jelly, and one bottle of Chili Sauce. Add about 1 cup of Sweet Baby Rays Sweet and Spicy BBQ sauce, and 2 Tbsp. of Jalapeno Salsa. It will cook up. Adjust the BBQ sauce if it needs a little more.\nIt all will make a difference, and everyone loves the way I make them.",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-07T11:49:52.630Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GentleRoll7926"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These tasted just like the classic recipe of ketchup and brown sugar. I used Sweet Baby Ray’s BBQ sauce and just a generic grape jelly. Instead of slow cooking I let the smokies simmer in the sauce on the stove for about 20 minutes until the sauce was nice and thick and the smokies well coated. I served them as an appetizer on Thanksgiving and everyone thought they were delicious, even the kids. Will be making this recipe again!",
            "datePublished": "2023-11-25T11:33:00.381Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lbuhlig1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like many others, I made this with chili sauce and grape jelly. I also added little meatballs and a can of drained pineapple chunks. Instead of the crockpot, I poured it all in a sauce pan and simmered on low for about 20 minutes. The sauce thickened up a bit, which we loved. I fixed a pouch of jasmine rice and poured the sausage mixture on top. It was delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-14T04:41:28.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ldysugrlpz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 2 packs of cocktail smokies, 1 big bottle of Sweet Baby Ray's BBQ sauce, and half a jar of Welch's grape jelly. I cooked it for 2 hours on low. There were only 2 smokies left when the company pot luck was over. I call it a win!",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-24T22:24:40.063Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "darby"
            },
            "reviewBody": "L O V E this recipe! This is an old timerecipe my family has been using for YEARS! Word to the wise- use a sweet bbq sauce (sweet baby rays is always a winner!) I use an entire 18oz BBQ bottle with a 12oz grape jelly. Love it!",
            "datePublished": "2017-12-31T22:43:26.277Z"
          },
